sn35.136:1.6 | S: tastes … | T: take pleasure in flavors…
sn35.136:1.7 | S: touches … | T: take pleasure in tactile sensations…
sn35.136:1.8 | S: ideas, they love them and enjoy them. | T: “Devas & human beings take pleasure in ideas, delight in ideas, rejoice in ideas.
sn35.136:1.9 | S: But when ideas perish, fade away, and cease, gods and humans live in suffering. | T: With the change, fading away, & cessation of ideas, devas & human beings dwell in suffering & stress.
sn35.136:1.10 | S: The Realized One has truly understood the origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape of sights, so he doesn’t like, love, or enjoy them. | T: “But the Tathāgata, monks—worthy & rightly self-awakened—knowing, as they have come to be, the origination, the disappearance, the allure, the drawbacks of—and escape from—forms, doesn’t take pleasure in forms, delight in forms, rejoice in forms.
sn35.136:1.11 | S: When sights perish, fade away, and cease, the Realized One lives happily. | T: With the change, fading away, & cessation of forms, the Tathāgata dwells happily.
sn35.136:1.12 | S: The Realized One has truly understood the origin, disappearance, gratification, drawback, and escape of sounds … | T: “Knowing, as they have come to be, the origination, the disappearance, the allure, the drawbacks of—and escape from—sounds…
sn35.136:1.13 | S: smells … | T: aromas…
sn35.136:1.14 | S: tastes … | T: flavors…
sn35.136:1.15 | S: touches … | T: tactile sensations…
sn35.136:1.16 | S: ideas, so he doesn’t like, love, or enjoy them. | T: “Knowing, as they have come to be, the origination, the disappearance, the allure, the drawbacks of—and escape from—ideas, he doesn’t take pleasure in ideas, delight in ideas, rejoice in ideas.

